00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:47.720
So what is the methodology
for goal-setting

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.810
that I can very much recommend
and really use for myself?

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.873
This methodology is called
objectives and key results, OKRs.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.440
And maybe you've already heard about it.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:59.750
It got quite popular in the last years

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:00.870
in the corporate world.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:04.490
To my knowledge, it was
first described by Andy Grove

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:07.160
in his book "High Output Management."

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:10.020
Andy Grove was the former Intel CEO.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.750
He wrote this book,
very worthwhile reading.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.970
He talks about lots of
other topics as well.

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:16.770
It is included in the link
in the video description

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:19.180
where I talk about my
book recommendations.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.120
So pick this up, very, very
big recommendation from me.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.770
But there is a chapter in here about MBO,

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.110
management by objectives,

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:29.130
which is a bit of an old
management methodology

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:31.520
that was quite popular several years ago.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.610
And out of these ideas,

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:35.180
the system of OKRs has
been developed over time.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.580
Today, OKRs are used by many startups,

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.910
but also larger corporations
like Google, Microsoft,

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.600
Twitter, Intel, and the like.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.610
Now, one could make a full
course about what OKRs are

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:48.360
and how to implement them,
but the basic idea is

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.070
that you break down your
goals into objectives.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:53.030
So this is the O of OKRs.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.990
But then you just
aggregate every objective

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.480
into some key results,
some clear, measurable,

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:00.960
key results that you want to achieve,

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.080
then together will lead
you towards this objective

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.690
that you set for yourself as a goal.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:08.050
Now, we will soon look
into a couple of examples

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:10.000
how I did this for myself.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.180
But just one other idea I
want you to understand is

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.010
that the idea is that the key results

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.600
that you set for yourself,
they should be stretch goals.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:17.860
They should be very ambitious.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:19.440
And the idea is that you should be okay

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.730
if you achieve 60 to
70% of that key result.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:25.120
So be bold, set some ambitious targets

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.790
which might be achievable,

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.260
but maybe where you would also be okay

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:31.410
if you're maybe only achieve
60 to 70% of them after all.

