00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:04.510
I always set for myself a net worth target

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.120
that then I break down by quarter.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:07.310
So if you've already watched some

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:10.270
of my other personal finance
related videos, for instance,

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.610
how I achieved the 50% savings rate

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:14.580
or my general strategy on investments,

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:16.010
you already know that this is a topic

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:17.310
that is very important to me.

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:18.180
And since I started

00:13:18.180 --> 00:13:21.140
to systematically track my net
worth a couple of years ago,

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:24.350
I feel like this alone has
helped me to really increase it,

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:26.010
to really just focus on it,

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:28.610
and making sure that this
number goes up over time.

00:13:28.610 --> 00:13:29.760
So if you've never heard about this,

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.250
what the net worth means is
pretty much just the difference

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:34.040
of the value of your assets,

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.110
so for instance, your stock portfolio,

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:37.780
some other investments
that you might have,

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:40.200
or anything else of
significant value that you own,

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:43.150
subtracted by all the liabilities

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:44.280
that you have on your name.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.500
So if you still have student
loans or some other debt

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:49.130
or maybe a mortgage on your
house, you would deduct that

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:52.160
from the value of your assets
to end up with your net worth.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:53.760
So I have a more complex spreadsheet

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:55.530
that I use to track my own net worth.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:57.480
So if you're interested to
see how this looks like,

00:13:57.480 --> 00:13:59.450
